<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hithadhoo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hithadhoo is the largest island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addu-atoll">Addu Atoll</a> in the southern Maldives and the administrative centre of Addu City. In 1959–1963 it served as the capital of the breakaway United Suvadive Republic under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-afeef">Abdullah Afeef</a>. It is linked by causeways to neighbouring islands of the atoll, including Gan.</p></div>
